        ]
      },
      "worked": "\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\dfrac{a(ax-b)-a(ax+b)}{(ax-b)^2}\\\\y'&=-\\dfrac{2ab}{(ax-b)^2}.\\end{align*}$$\n\n The parameters have opposite signs, so $ab<0$. Also $(ax-b)^2>0$ at every point on the curve. Hence $y'>0$, and every tangent has positive gradient.",
